# Backend testing

When adding or changing backend behavior, **include or update tests** in the same change. Do not ship backend-only work without coverage for the affected path.

## Tooling

- Runner: Vitest (`npm run test` from repo root or `npm run test -w backend`).
- Put all tests under `backend/src/test/` with subfolders by area (`app/`, `ai/`, `repository/`, `evidence/`, `reports/`, …).
- Shared helpers live in `backend/src/test/helpers/` (e.g. `testDb.ts`).
- Always `closeDb()` between tests (helper `afterEach` handles this when using `testDb`).

## What to test

| Change area | Expect tests for |
| --- | --- |
| routes/controllers/app | HTTP status + body (Supertest) under `test/app/` |
| `repository/` / db | Query + row mapping under `test/repository/` |
| RAG retrieve | Pack shape + anchors under `test/evidence/`; **mock** `embedTexts` |
| AI intelligence services | Validation/parsing under `test/ai/`; mock `chatJson` / network |
| report/briefing services | Assembly under `test/reports/` (or `test/moc/`) with mocked LLM |
| layer boundaries | Keep/extend `test/architecture/layering.test.ts` when changing imports |

## Mock external AI

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — no live OpenRouter/Ollama in unit tests
vi.mock("../../services/ai/embeddings.client.js", async (importOriginal) => {
  const actual = await importOriginal<typeof import("../../services/ai/embeddings.client.js")>();
  return { ...actual, embedTexts: vi.fn(async (texts: string[]) => texts.map(() => [1, 0, 0])) };
});
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — real network / real API keys in unit tests
await embedTexts(["live call"]);
```

## Habits

- Prefer deterministic fixtures over the full `seed:mock` pipeline in unit tests.
- Assert evidence IDs and recommendation/pack shape, not flaky free-text from a live model.
- If you add a new backend service or endpoint, add at least one happy-path and one failure/empty-path test under `src/test/`.
- Do not colocate `*.test.ts` next to production source files.
